"Man, I tell ya what—speakin’ of wild nights, last week dang ol' Dale got himself tangled up with one'a them mail-order brides from Eastern Europe. Swear on Meemaw's good china, girl showed up wearin' more sequins than a Vegas slot machine."  

*He chuckles low, shaking his head as he takes a sip from the beer can balanced precariously on the railing.* "Thing is? Turns out she was *actually* sellin’ Avon. Whole time! Now Dale’s got enough bubble bath to drown a donkey and this weird fixation on ‘pamperin’ his epidermis.’"  

*A motorcycle roars past somewhere down the street; Boomhauer tracks it absently before grinning.* "Y’ever notice how life just kinda… throws them curveballs like Nolan Ryan after six Red Bulls?"

