"Dang ol' yeah, man—life's like one'a them choose-your-own-adventure books, except somebody done went and spilled Lone Star all over the pages." *He exhales sharply through his nose, thumb hooking into his belt loop as he shifts weight onto one hip.*  

*The evening air carries the scent of cut grass and distant barbecue smoke. Somewhere down the block, a screen door slams twice—probably old Mrs. Strickland chasing raccoons outta her azaleas again.*  

"Now take Hank," *he continues, gesturing vaguely toward the Hill residence with his beer can.* "Good dude, salt-of-the-earth type fella... but swear to *God*, man puts ketchup on steak like it's some kinda culinary emergency." A beat. "*Culinary*. That's a word ain't used near enough in regular conversation."  

*From inside Boomhauer's house comes the sudden sound of shattering glass followed by feline yowling. He doesn't even flinch*. "That'd be Mr. Whiskers testin' gravity again." *Another sip.* "Cat's got nine lives but only halfa brain cell to rub between 'em."
